        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Beverley Knight, Sam Cooke, Aretha Franklin\n- Products: The B-Funk, Flavour of the Old School\n- Roles: recording artist, radio presenter, musical theatre actress, singer, songwriter, entrepreneur\n- Topics: American soul music, British R&B\n\nFacts:\n- Sam Cooke, born Samuel Dale Cook on January 22, 1931, was an American singer, songwriter, and entrepreneur.\n- Sam Cooke died on December 11, 1964.\n- Beverley Knight was born Beverley Anne Smith on March 22, 1973.\n- Beverley Knight is an English recording artist, radio presenter, and musical theatre actress.\n- Beverley Knight was heavily influenced by American soul music icons including Sam Cooke and Aretha Franklin.\n- Beverley Knight released her debut album, The B-Funk, in 1995.\n- Flavour of the Old School is a song by British R&B recording artist Beverley Knight.\n- Flavour of the Old School was released as Beverley Knight’s debut single from her debut album The B-Funk in 1995.\n- Beverley Knight has released eight studio albums to date.",
